1
00:00:01,438 --> 00:00:04,317
It's a sanctuary base! Deep-space
exploration. Welcome to hell. . .

2
00:00:04,357 --> 00:00:07,263
What are you lot doing here? That's
a black hole. That's impossible.

3
00:00:07,392 --> 00:00:09,071
What are you lot doing here? That's
a black hole. That's impossible.

4
00:00:09,111 --> 00:00:12,788
This lump of rock is suspended
in perpetual geostationary orbit

5
00:00:12,828 --> 00:00:16,218
around that black hole,
without falling in.

6
00:00:16,258 --> 00:00:18,738
Some sort of power source is
holding us here.

7
00:00:18,778 --> 00:00:21,195
We're drilling down
to try and find it.

8
00:00:22,617 --> 00:00:24,451
The Tardis is gone.

9
00:00:24,491 --> 00:00:27,132
Whatever it is,
it's not a natural phenomenon.

10
00:00:27,172 --> 00:00:29,770
Some form of civilisation.

11
00:00:29,810 --> 00:00:31,488
They buried something.

12
00:00:34,244 --> 00:00:37,680
What are they called? .
They're the Ood, basic slave race.

13
00:00:37,720 --> 00:00:40,278
There's something happening
with the Ood. . .

14
00:00:40,318 --> 00:00:42,576
And you will worship him.

15
00:00:46,106 --> 00:00:50,265
You can tell Toby what we've found
is civilisation.

16
00:00:50,305 --> 00:00:53,781
These are the words of the beast. . .
and he has woken.

17
00:00:53,821 --> 00:00:57,137
I have been imprisoned
for eternity.

18
00:00:57,177 --> 00:00:59,057
But no more.

19
00:00:59,097 --> 00:01:02,133
The pit is open!

20
00:01:02,173 --> 00:01:05,489
And I am free!

21
00:01:43,648 --> 00:01:45,331
Open fire!

22
00:01:51,882 --> 00:01:54,119
We're stabilising!

23
00:01:54,159 --> 00:01:56,496
We've got orbit.

24
00:02:00,871 --> 00:02:03,667
Doctor?

25
00:02:03,707 --> 00:02:06,739
Doctor, can you hear me?
Doctor, Ida, are you there?

26
00:02:07,906 --> 00:02:09,579
It's me!

27
00:02:09,619 --> 00:02:12,859
But they're coming. It's the Ood.

28
00:02:12,899 --> 00:02:14,697
They've gone mad. How many of them?

29
00:02:14,737 --> 00:02:18,411
All of them, all 50. Danny,
out of the way. Out of the way!

30
00:02:18,451 --> 00:02:20,931
But they're armed!
It's the interface device.

31
00:02:20,971 --> 00:02:24,207
I don't know how,
but they're using it as a weapon.

32
00:02:26,245 --> 00:02:28,418
A-A-A-A-Aaah!

33
00:02:30,959 --> 00:02:32,893
Close Door One.

34
00:02:41,747 --> 00:02:44,984
Open Door One. Close Door One.

35
00:02:45,024 --> 00:02:47,179
Lockdown! Seal Door One!

36
00:02:50,537 --> 00:02:52,215
Jefferson, what's happening?

37
00:02:52,255 --> 00:02:55,892
I've got very little ammunition,
sir, how about you?

38
00:02:55,932 --> 00:02:58,409
All I've got is a bolt-gun.

39
00:02:58,449 --> 00:03:00,686
With, uh. . .all of one bolt.

40
00:03:00,726 --> 00:03:04,642
I could take out a grand total of
one Ood, fat lot of good that is( !)

41
00:03:04,682 --> 00:03:07,600
Given the emergency,
I'd recommend. . .Strategy Nine.

42
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:12,594
Strategy Nine, agreed. Right, we
need to get everyone together. Rose?

43
00:03:12,634 --> 00:03:16,387
What about Ida and the Doctor,
any word? I can't get a reply.

44
00:03:16,427 --> 00:03:18,866
Just. . . nothing.
I keep trying, but it's. . .

45
00:03:18,906 --> 00:03:22,061
No, sorry, I'm fine, still here!

46
00:03:22,101 --> 00:03:25,020
Oh, you could've said, you stupid. . .

47
00:03:25,060 --> 00:03:29,060
Woah. Careful. Anyway!
It's both of us, me and Ida, hello!

48
00:03:29,100 --> 00:03:31,613
But the seal opened up.

49
00:03:31,653 --> 00:03:33,971
It's gone.

50
00:03:34,011 --> 00:03:36,851
All we've got left is this. . .chasm.

51
00:03:36,891 --> 00:03:39,769
'How deep is it?' Can't tell.

52
00:03:39,809 --> 00:03:42,325
Looks like it goes down forever.
'The Pit is open. '

53
00:03:42,365 --> 00:03:47,878
That's what the voice said.
But there's nothing. . . I mean,
there's nothing coming out?

54
00:03:47,918 --> 00:03:50,555
No, no sign of the Beast.

55
00:03:50,595 --> 00:03:53,189
It said Satan.
Come on, Rose. Keep it together.

56
00:03:53,229 --> 00:03:55,407
Is there no such thing?

57
00:03:56,706 --> 00:03:58,343
Doctor.

58
00:03:58,383 --> 00:04:01,621
'Doctor, tell me
there's no such thing. '

59
00:04:01,661 --> 00:04:05,299
Ida. I recommend that you
withdraw, immediately.

60
00:04:05,339 --> 00:04:10,133
But we've come all this way. . . !
OK, that was an order. Withdraw!

61
00:04:10,173 --> 00:04:12,570
When that opened,
the whole planet shifted.

62
00:04:12,610 --> 00:04:15,970
One more inch, and we fall into
the black hole. This stops, now.

63
00:04:16,010 --> 00:04:18,767
But it's not much better up there,
with the Ood.

64
00:04:18,807 --> 00:04:20,564
I'm initiating Strategy Nine,

65
00:04:20,604 --> 00:04:24,785
so I need the two of you
back up top, immediately, no arg. . .

66
00:04:25,638 --> 00:04:28,794
Ida. IDA? !

67
00:04:28,834 --> 00:04:30,909
What do you think?

68
00:04:30,949 --> 00:04:33,149
He gave an order.

69
00:04:33,189 --> 00:04:36,596
Yeah, but what do YOU think?

70
00:04:39,069 --> 00:04:42,470
It said, "I am the temptation. "

71
00:04:45,143 --> 00:04:47,774
If there's something in there. . .

72
00:04:47,814 --> 00:04:50,650
Why's it still hiding?

73
00:04:50,690 --> 00:04:56,016
Maybe we've opened the prison,
but not the cell.

74
00:04:56,056 --> 00:04:58,943
We should go down.

75
00:04:58,983 --> 00:05:01,275
I'd go.

76
00:05:02,420 --> 00:05:06,800
What about you? Ohh, in a second.
But then again. . .

77
00:05:08,689 --> 00:05:10,687
That is so human.

78
00:05:10,727 --> 00:05:13,724
Where angels fear to tread.

79
00:05:14,806 --> 00:05:17,309
Even now, standing on the edge.

80
00:05:18,803 --> 00:05:21,877
It's that feeling you get, yeah?

81
00:05:21,917 --> 00:05:24,514
Right at the back of your head,

82
00:05:24,554 --> 00:05:26,951
that impulse,

83
00:05:26,991 --> 00:05:30,027
that strange little impulse,

84
00:05:30,067 --> 00:05:35,585
that mad little voice saying,
"Go on, go on, go on,

85
00:05:35,625 --> 00:05:37,803
"go over, go on. . . "

86
00:05:39,699 --> 00:05:41,997
Maybe it's relying on that.

87
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:47,528
For once in my life, Officer Scott,

88
00:05:47,568 --> 00:05:50,110
I'm going to say. . .

89
00:05:51,484 --> 00:05:53,482
Retreat.

90
00:05:53,522 --> 00:05:55,562
Ohh.

91
00:05:55,602 --> 00:05:57,638
Now I know I'm getting old.

92
00:05:57,678 --> 00:05:59,235
Rose. We're coming back.

93
00:05:59,275 --> 00:06:01,796
Best news I've heard all day.

94
00:06:01,836 --> 00:06:04,512
What are you doing?

95
00:06:04,552 --> 00:06:07,670
He's infected. He brought that
thing on board - you saw it.

96
00:06:07,710 --> 00:06:13,264
Are you gonna start shooting your
own people now, is that what you're
gonna do? Is it? If necessary.

97
00:06:13,304 --> 00:06:17,030
Well, then, you'll have to shoot me.
If necessary. So what's it gonna be?

98
00:06:19,378 --> 00:06:22,812
Look at his face.
Whatever it was, it's gone.

99
00:06:22,852 --> 00:06:25,064
It passed into the Ood,
you saw it happen.

100
00:06:25,888 --> 00:06:28,345
He's clean.

101
00:06:29,926 --> 00:06:33,003
Any sign of trouble, I'll shoot him.

102
00:06:33,043 --> 00:06:35,919
You all right?

103
00:06:35,959 --> 00:06:38,637
Yeah.

104
00:06:38,677 --> 00:06:42,270
Um. Dunno. Can you remember anything?
Just. . .

105
00:06:42,310 --> 00:06:44,308
It was so angry.

106
00:06:44,348 --> 00:06:48,733
It was fury, and rage, and. . .death.

107
00:06:51,383 --> 00:06:54,060
It was him.

108
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,417
It was the Devil.

109
00:06:56,457 --> 00:06:59,079
Come on.

110
00:07:04,688 --> 00:07:08,202
What's Strategy Nine?
Open the airlocks.

111
00:07:08,242 --> 00:07:13,996
We'll be safe inside the lockdown.
The Ood will get thrown out,
into the vacuum.

112
00:07:14,036 --> 00:07:16,396
So we're going back to a slaughter.

113
00:07:16,436 --> 00:07:18,239
The Devil's work.

114
00:07:19,632 --> 00:07:23,068
'OK, we're in. Bring us up. '

115
00:07:23,108 --> 00:07:29,052
Ascension, in three, two, one.

116
00:07:35,052 --> 00:07:38,012
'This is the darkness. '

117
00:07:38,052 --> 00:07:39,808
This is my domain.

118
00:07:39,848 --> 00:07:44,207
You little things
that live in the light,

119
00:07:44,247 --> 00:07:46,963
clinging to your feeble suns,

120
00:07:47,003 --> 00:07:49,399
which die, in the end. . .

121
00:07:49,439 --> 00:07:52,397
That's not the Ood.
Something is talking through them.

122
00:07:52,437 --> 00:07:55,194
Only the darkness remains.

123
00:07:55,234 --> 00:07:59,269
This is Captain Zachary Cross Flane,
of Sanctuary Base Six,

124
00:07:59,309 --> 00:08:04,145
representing the Torchwood Archive.
You will identify yourself.

125
00:08:04,185 --> 00:08:06,182
You know my name.

126
00:08:06,222 --> 00:08:07,702
What do you want?

127
00:08:07,742 --> 00:08:10,539
You will die here. All of you.

128
00:08:10,579 --> 00:08:12,814
This planet is your grave.

129
00:08:12,854 --> 00:08:15,212
It's him. It's him. It's him.

130
00:08:15,252 --> 00:08:18,448
If you are the Beast,
then answer me this. Which one?

131
00:08:18,488 --> 00:08:21,605
Cos the universe has been busy
since you've been gone.

132
00:08:21,645 --> 00:08:24,122
There's more religions
than there are planets.

133
00:08:24,162 --> 00:08:28,595
The Arkiphets, Quoldonity,
Christianity, Pash-Pash,

134
00:08:28,635 --> 00:08:32,434
New Judaism, San Claar,
the Church of the Tin Vagabond. . .

135
00:08:32,474 --> 00:08:34,553
Which Devil are you? All of them.

136
00:08:34,593 --> 00:08:38,028
What, then you're the truth
behind the myth(? )

137
00:08:38,068 --> 00:08:39,987
This one knows me.

138
00:08:40,027 --> 00:08:44,981
As I know him.
The killer of his own kind.

139
00:08:46,061 --> 00:08:48,015
How did you end up on this rock?

140
00:08:48,055 --> 00:08:51,853
The Disciples of the Light
rose up against me,

141
00:08:51,893 --> 00:08:55,490
and chained me in the Pit
for all eternity.

142
00:08:55,530 --> 00:08:58,607
When was this? Before time.

143
00:08:58,647 --> 00:09:02,162
What does that mean? Before time.

144
00:09:02,202 --> 00:09:04,001
What does "before time" MEAN?

145
00:09:04,041 --> 00:09:08,798
Before time and light
and space and matter.

146
00:09:08,838 --> 00:09:11,514
Before the cataclysm.

147
00:09:11,554 --> 00:09:14,913
Before this universe was created.

148
00:09:14,953 --> 00:09:17,988
That's impossible. No life
could have existed back then.

149
00:09:18,028 --> 00:09:20,980
Is that your religion?

150
00:09:22,183 --> 00:09:25,661
It's a belief. You know nothing.

151
00:09:25,701 --> 00:09:28,414
All of you, so small.

152
00:09:28,454 --> 00:09:32,409
The Captain, so scared of command.

153
00:09:32,449 --> 00:09:37,805
The soldier,
haunted by the eyes of his wife.

154
00:09:37,845 --> 00:09:42,720
The scientist,
still running from Daddy.

155
00:09:42,760 --> 00:09:45,997
The little boy who lied.

156
00:09:46,037 --> 00:09:48,274
The virgin.

157
00:09:48,314 --> 00:09:50,672
And the lost girl.

158
00:09:50,712 --> 00:09:53,790
So far away from home.

159
00:09:53,830 --> 00:09:59,782
The valiant child
who will die in battle, so very soon.

160
00:09:59,822 --> 00:10:01,862
Doctor, what does that mean?

161
00:10:01,902 --> 00:10:04,215
Rose, don't listen.
What does it mean? !

162
00:10:04,255 --> 00:10:07,092
You will die. . .

163
00:10:07,132 --> 00:10:09,834
. .and I will live.

164
00:10:12,007 --> 00:10:13,767
What the hell was that?

165
00:10:13,807 --> 00:10:16,564
I had that thing inside my head!

166
00:10:16,604 --> 00:10:18,641
Doctor, what did it mean?

167
00:10:18,681 --> 00:10:22,238
What do we do? Jefferson, Zack,
what do we do? Captain. . . ?

168
00:10:22,278 --> 00:10:26,073
The orbit, the planet,
the black hole - everything's true.

169
00:10:26,113 --> 00:10:28,192
How did it know that?
Did anyone. . . ?

170
00:10:28,232 --> 00:10:32,288
What battle? What did it mean? Stop!
What do we do?

171
00:10:35,784 --> 00:10:39,696
If you want voices in the dark,
listen to mine.
It's playing on basic fears.

172
00:10:39,736 --> 00:10:45,651
Darkness, childhood, nightmares,
all that stuff. But that's how the
Devil works. Or a good psychologist.

173
00:10:45,691 --> 00:10:47,969
How did it know about my father?

174
00:10:48,009 --> 00:10:51,566
OK. But what makes his version
of the truth any better than mine?

175
00:10:51,606 --> 00:10:55,048
Cos I'll tell you what I can see.
Humans. Brilliant humans.

176
00:10:55,088 --> 00:10:58,880
Humans who travelled
all the way across space,
flying in a tiny rocket,

177
00:10:58,920 --> 00:11:02,515
into the orbit of a black hole,
just for the sake of discovery!

178
00:11:02,555 --> 00:11:05,514
That's amazing! D'you hear me?
Amazing.

179
00:11:05,554 --> 00:11:08,272
All of you. The captain.
His officer. His elder.

180
00:11:08,312 --> 00:11:10,028
His juniors. His friends.

181
00:11:10,068 --> 00:11:14,662
All with one advantage.
The Beast is alone. We are not.

182
00:11:14,702 --> 00:11:17,119
If we can use that
to fight against him. . .

183
00:11:21,733 --> 00:11:24,031
The cable snapped! Get out!

184
00:11:31,724 --> 00:11:34,081
Doctor, we lost the cable!

185
00:11:34,121 --> 00:11:36,959
Doctor, are you all right? Doctor?

186
00:11:36,999 --> 00:11:39,237
Comms are down.
(Doctor, can you hear me? )

187
00:11:39,277 --> 00:11:42,433
I've still got life-signs,
but. . .we've lost the capsule.

188
00:11:42,473 --> 00:11:44,990
There's no way out.

189
00:11:45,030 --> 00:11:46,833
They're stuck down there.

190
00:11:51,384 --> 00:11:53,457
How much air have we got?

191
00:11:53,497 --> 00:11:56,698
60 minutes.

192
00:11:56,738 --> 00:11:58,336
55.

193
00:11:59,535 --> 00:12:01,373
But we've got to bring them back!

194
00:12:01,413 --> 00:12:04,809
They're ten miles down. We haven't
got another ten miles of cable.

195
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:08,415
Captain?

196
00:12:09,484 --> 00:12:11,160
Situation report.

197
00:12:24,908 --> 00:12:26,626
It's the Ood.

198
00:12:26,666 --> 00:12:30,103
They're cutting through
the door-bolts, they're breaking in.

199
00:12:30,143 --> 00:12:32,977
Yes, same on Door 25.
How long's it gonna take?

200
00:12:33,017 --> 00:12:36,788
Well, it's only a basic frame,
should take ten minutes.

201
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:39,656
Eight.

202
00:12:41,129 --> 00:12:43,928
I've got a security frame -
it might last a bit longer.

203
00:12:43,968 --> 00:12:48,402
But that doesn't help you.
Right. So! We've got to stop them,
or get out, or both.

204
00:12:48,442 --> 00:12:50,919
I'll take both, yeah, but how? !

205
00:12:50,959 --> 00:12:54,041
You heard the Doctor. Why d'you
think that thing cut him off?

206
00:12:54,081 --> 00:12:57,913
Cos he was making sense,
he was telling you to think
your way out of this!

207
00:12:57,953 --> 00:13:00,231
Come on! For starters,
we need some light.

208
00:13:00,271 --> 00:13:04,547
Zack, there's got to be
some sort of power, somewhere.
There's nothing I can do.

209
00:13:04,587 --> 00:13:07,384
Some Captain!
Stuck in here, pressing buttons.

210
00:13:07,424 --> 00:13:12,176
But that's what the Doctor meant!
Press the right buttons!
They've gutted the generators!

211
00:13:12,216 --> 00:13:15,813
But. . .the rocket's
got an independent supply.

212
00:13:15,853 --> 00:13:18,210
If I can reroute that. . .

213
00:13:18,250 --> 00:13:21,287
Mr Jefferson!
Open the bypass conduits,

214
00:13:21,327 --> 00:13:23,684
override the safety.

215
00:13:23,724 --> 00:13:27,084
Opening bypass conduits, sir!

216
00:13:27,124 --> 00:13:30,118
Channeling rocket feed.

217
00:13:30,158 --> 00:13:35,194
In three, two, one.

218
00:13:35,234 --> 00:13:37,996
Power!

219
00:13:38,036 --> 00:13:41,668
There we go! Let there be light!
What about that Strategy Nine thing?

220
00:13:41,708 --> 00:13:43,826
Not enough power - needs 100%.

221
00:13:43,866 --> 00:13:47,498
Right. We need a way out. Zack,
Mr Jefferson, start working on that.

222
00:13:47,538 --> 00:13:49,897
Toby, what about you?
I'm not a soldier!

223
00:13:49,937 --> 00:13:53,171
No, you're the archaeologist.
What do you know about the Pit?

224
00:13:53,211 --> 00:13:56,892
We can't even translate the language,
but. . . Hold on. Maybe. . .

225
00:13:56,932 --> 00:13:59,048
What is it?

226
00:13:59,088 --> 00:14:03,482
Since that thing was inside my head,
the letters make more sense.

227
00:14:03,522 --> 00:14:08,199
Then get to work. Anything
you can translate, just. . .anything.

228
00:14:08,239 --> 00:14:12,153
As for you, Danny boy,
you're in charge of the Ood.
Any way of stopping them?

229
00:14:12,193 --> 00:14:14,311
Well. . . I don't know.

230
00:14:14,351 --> 00:14:16,510
Then find out!

231
00:14:16,550 --> 00:14:21,834
Sooner we get control of this base,
the sooner we can get the
Doctor out. Now get going. Shift!

232
00:14:27,139 --> 00:14:31,253
We've got all this cable,
might as well use it.

233
00:14:31,293 --> 00:14:36,047
The drum's disconnected,
we could adapt it. Feed it through. . .

234
00:14:36,087 --> 00:14:38,284
And then what?

235
00:14:38,324 --> 00:14:40,164
Abseil.

236
00:14:40,204 --> 00:14:42,280
Into the Pit.

237
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,038
Abseil! Right!

238
00:14:44,078 --> 00:14:47,758
We're running out of air, with no way
back. It's the only thing we CAN do.

239
00:14:47,798 --> 00:14:51,192
Even if it's the last thing
we ever achieve.

240
00:14:51,232 --> 00:14:53,829
I'll get back. Rose is up there.

241
00:14:53,869 --> 00:14:58,786
Then maybe the key to that
is finding out what's in the Pit.

242
00:14:58,826 --> 00:15:02,139
Well. It's half of a good plan.

243
00:15:02,179 --> 00:15:03,939
What's the other half?

244
00:15:03,979 --> 00:15:06,806
I go down. Not you.

245
00:15:08,292 --> 00:15:12,797
Junctions 5, 6, 7. . .

246
00:15:15,086 --> 00:15:17,748
Re-route filters 16 to 24. Go.

247
00:15:19,764 --> 00:15:22,839
There's all sorts of viruses
that could stop the Ood.

248
00:15:22,879 --> 00:15:25,676
Trouble is,
we haven't got them on board.

249
00:15:25,716 --> 00:15:28,394
Well, that's handy,
listing things we haven't got.

250
00:15:28,434 --> 00:15:31,136
We haven't got a swimming pool
either, or a Tesco.

251
00:15:32,751 --> 00:15:36,221
Oh, my God, it says yes!
I can do it!

252
00:15:36,261 --> 00:15:40,739
Hypothetically, if you flip
the monitor, broadcast a flare,

253
00:15:40,779 --> 00:15:44,253
it can disrupt the telepathy.
Brainstorm ! What happens to the Ood?

254
00:15:44,293 --> 00:15:46,053
It'll tank them, spark-out!

255
00:15:46,093 --> 00:15:48,369
There we are then - do it!

256
00:15:48,409 --> 00:15:53,127
No, but I'd have to transmit
from the central monitor.

257
00:15:53,167 --> 00:15:56,369
We need to go to Ood Habitation.

258
00:15:58,042 --> 00:16:00,119
That's what we'll do then.

259
00:16:00,159 --> 00:16:03,636
Mr Jefferson, sir, any way out?

260
00:16:03,676 --> 00:16:06,513
Just about. There's a network
of maintenance tunnels

261
00:16:06,553 --> 00:16:09,070
running underneath the base.

262
00:16:09,110 --> 00:16:13,304
Ventilation shafts!
I appreciate the reference,
but there's no ventilation.

263
00:16:13,344 --> 00:16:17,778
No air, in fact - they were designed
for machines, not lifeforms.

264
00:16:17,818 --> 00:16:21,694
But I can manipulate
the oxygen field from here,

265
00:16:21,734 --> 00:16:24,013
create discrete pockets
of atmosphere.

266
00:16:24,053 --> 00:16:28,049
If I control it manually, I can
follow you through the network.

267
00:16:28,089 --> 00:16:32,683
Right! So. . . We go down, and
you make the air follow us? By hand?

268
00:16:32,723 --> 00:16:35,843
You wanted me pressing buttons.
Yep. I asked for it. OK.

269
00:16:35,883 --> 00:16:38,425
We need to get to Ood Habitation.
Work out a route.

270
00:16:40,477 --> 00:16:42,433
That should hold it.

271
00:16:42,473 --> 00:16:45,792
How's it going? Fine. Should work.

272
00:16:45,832 --> 00:16:48,625
Doesn't feel like
such a good idea now.

273
00:16:51,142 --> 00:16:54,340
There it is again. That itch.

274
00:16:54,380 --> 00:16:56,656
Go down, go down,
go down, go down. . .

275
00:16:56,696 --> 00:17:01,293
The urge to jump. D'you know where
it comes from, that sensation?

276
00:17:01,333 --> 00:17:06,048
Genetic heritage, ever since
we were primates in the trees.

277
00:17:06,088 --> 00:17:08,525
It's our body's way of testing us,

278
00:17:08,565 --> 00:17:12,881
calculating whether or not
we can reach the next branch.

279
00:17:12,921 --> 00:17:15,159
No, that's not it.

280
00:17:15,199 --> 00:17:17,117
That's too kind.

281
00:17:17,157 --> 00:17:20,876
It's not the urge to jump,
it's deeper than that.

282
00:17:20,916 --> 00:17:22,632
It's the urge to fall.

283
00:17:22,672 --> 00:17:25,499
Doctor!

284
00:17:26,909 --> 00:17:29,384
You OK? Not bad, thanks.

285
00:17:29,424 --> 00:17:33,738
Wall of the Pit seems to be
the same as the cavern,

286
00:17:33,778 --> 00:17:36,055
just. . . not much of it.

287
00:17:36,095 --> 00:17:41,015
There's a crust about 20ft down,
and then. . .

288
00:17:42,410 --> 00:17:44,503
Nothing. Just the Pit.

289
00:17:45,847 --> 00:17:48,444
OK, then. Lower me down.

290
00:17:48,484 --> 00:17:50,093
Here we go, then.

291
00:17:58,274 --> 00:18:01,511
Danny! Hold on, just conforming.

292
00:18:01,551 --> 00:18:04,628
Danny, we've got to go now! Come on!

293
00:18:05,668 --> 00:18:09,779
There! Put that into the monitor
and it's a bad time to be an Ood!

294
00:18:09,819 --> 00:18:11,297
We're coming back, got that?

295
00:18:11,337 --> 00:18:13,977
We're coming back
and getting the Doctor out.

296
00:18:14,017 --> 00:18:17,494
OK, Danny, you go first, then you,
then Toby. I'll go last.

297
00:18:17,534 --> 00:18:19,337
Now come on, quick as you can.

298
00:18:23,089 --> 00:18:26,925
God, it stinks. You all right?
Yeah, laughing( !)

299
00:18:26,965 --> 00:18:30,816
Which way do we go? Just go straight
ahead, keep going till I say so.

300
00:18:37,873 --> 00:18:41,305
Not your best angle, Danny. Oi.
Stop it!

301
00:18:41,345 --> 00:18:43,603
I dunno, could be worse. Oi!

302
00:18:44,585 --> 00:18:47,941
Straight on till you find
Junction 7.1. Keep breathing.

303
00:18:47,981 --> 00:18:51,547
I'm feeding you air. I've got you.

304
00:19:04,923 --> 00:19:07,200
We're at 7.1, sir.

305
00:19:07,240 --> 00:19:09,054
OK, I've got you.

306
00:19:11,638 --> 00:19:13,994
I'm just aerating the next section.

307
00:19:14,034 --> 00:19:17,191
Getting kinda cramped, sir.
Can't you hurry it up?

308
00:19:17,231 --> 00:19:19,987
I'm working on half-power here.
Stop complaining.

309
00:19:20,027 --> 00:19:22,903
Mr Jefferson said, stop complaining.
I heard. He heard.

310
00:19:22,943 --> 00:19:26,464
The air's getting a bit thin.
HE's complaining now. I heard.

311
00:19:28,497 --> 00:19:31,694
Danny, is that you?
I'm not exactly happy!

312
00:19:31,734 --> 00:19:35,129
I'm just moving the air, I've got
to oxygenate the next section.

313
00:19:35,169 --> 00:19:38,208
Now, keep calm,
or it's gonna feel worse.

314
00:19:41,645 --> 00:19:45,003
What was that? Mr Jefferson,
what was that? What was that noise?

315
00:19:45,043 --> 00:19:47,119
Captain. What was that?

316
00:19:47,159 --> 00:19:51,873
The junction in Habitation Five's
been opened. It must be the Ood.

317
00:19:51,913 --> 00:19:56,467
They're in the tunnels.
Well, open the gate! I've got to
get the air in! Just open it, sir!

318
00:19:56,507 --> 00:19:59,904
Where are they, are they close?
I can't tell, I can't see them.

319
00:19:59,944 --> 00:20:02,862
The computer doesn't register Ood
as proper lifeforms.

320
00:20:02,902 --> 00:20:05,569
Whose idea was that? ! Open the GATE!

321
00:20:09,612 --> 00:20:12,274
Danny, turn left, immediate left!

322
00:20:16,006 --> 00:20:19,444
The Ood, sir - can't you trap them,
cut off the air?

323
00:20:19,484 --> 00:20:22,390
Not without cutting off yours.

324
00:20:26,035 --> 00:20:30,711
Danny, turn right, go right. . .
Go faster, they're gonna catch up!

325
00:20:30,751 --> 00:20:34,786
I'll maintain defensive position.
You can't stop!

326
00:20:34,826 --> 00:20:38,821
Miss Tyler, that's my job. You've
got your task - now see to it!

327
00:20:38,861 --> 00:20:41,528
You heard what he said, now shift!

328
00:20:57,766 --> 00:21:00,600
8.2. Open 8.2.

329
00:21:00,640 --> 00:21:03,077
Zack, open 8.2!

330
00:21:03,117 --> 00:21:05,594
I've got to aerate it. Open it NOW!

331
00:21:05,634 --> 00:21:08,794
I'm TRYING!

332
00:21:08,834 --> 00:21:10,947
Danny, stop it, that's not helping!

333
00:21:10,987 --> 00:21:13,024
Zack! Get it open!

334
00:21:13,064 --> 00:21:16,821
Jefferson, I've got to open 8.2
by closing 8.1.

335
00:21:16,861 --> 00:21:20,537
You've got to get past the junction!
Now, move!

336
00:21:20,577 --> 00:21:23,290
That's an order! Now, move!

337
00:21:26,574 --> 00:21:30,999
I'm gonna lose oxygen, Jefferson,
I can't stop the automatics!

338
00:21:33,805 --> 00:21:36,282
That's it, come on, come on!

339
00:21:36,322 --> 00:21:39,359
Danny, turn left.
Head for 9.2, that's the last one.

340
00:21:39,399 --> 00:21:42,316
Jefferson,
you've got to move faster!

341
00:21:42,356 --> 00:21:45,273
John! Move! MOVE! Mr Jefferson!

342
00:21:45,313 --> 00:21:48,140
Come on! KEEP GOING!

343
00:21:51,903 --> 00:21:54,181
'Regret to inform you, sir.

344
00:21:54,221 --> 00:21:56,378
'I was a bit slow.

345
00:21:56,418 --> 00:21:58,777
'Not so fast, these days. '

346
00:21:58,817 --> 00:22:01,215
I can't open 8.1, John.

347
00:22:01,255 --> 00:22:03,772
Not without losing
air for the others.

348
00:22:03,812 --> 00:22:05,649
And quite right too, sir.

349
00:22:05,689 --> 00:22:07,947
I think I bought them a little time.

350
00:22:09,766 --> 00:22:12,284
'There's nothing I can do, John. '

351
00:22:12,324 --> 00:22:14,360
I'm sorry.

352
00:22:14,400 --> 00:22:18,557
You've done enough, sir.
Made a very good captain,
under the circumstances.

353
00:22:18,597 --> 00:22:23,474
Might I ask, if you can't
add oxygen to this section,

354
00:22:23,514 --> 00:22:27,064
can you speed up the
process of its removal?

355
00:22:27,104 --> 00:22:29,703
I don't understand. What d'you mean?

356
00:22:29,743 --> 00:22:33,219
Well, if I might choose
the manner of my departure, sir,

357
00:22:33,259 --> 00:22:36,376
lack of air
seems more natural than. . .

358
00:22:36,416 --> 00:22:42,090
Well, let's say, death by Ood.

359
00:22:42,130 --> 00:22:44,888
I'd appreciate it, sir.

360
00:22:44,928 --> 00:22:47,167
Godspeed, Mr Jefferson.

361
00:22:47,207 --> 00:22:49,920
Thank you, sir.

362
00:22:58,995 --> 00:23:04,186
Report.
Officer John Maynard Jefferson, PKD

363
00:23:04,226 --> 00:23:08,381
deceased, with honours,

364
00:23:08,421 --> 00:23:11,941
43K 2.1.

365
00:23:11,981 --> 00:23:13,819
Zack.

366
00:23:13,859 --> 00:23:16,335
We're at the final junction.

367
00:23:16,375 --> 00:23:19,652
9.2.

368
00:23:19,692 --> 00:23:21,849
And, uh. . .

369
00:23:21,889 --> 00:23:25,527
If my respects could be on record,
he saved our lives.

370
00:23:25,567 --> 00:23:30,191
Noted. Opening 9.2.

371
00:23:32,798 --> 00:23:36,314
Lower 9.2! Zack, LOWER IT!
Back back back!

372
00:23:36,354 --> 00:23:40,000
We can't go back, 8.2's sealed off -
we're stuck!

373
00:23:41,029 --> 00:23:43,452
Come on! UP!

374
00:23:50,257 --> 00:23:52,430
Come on! Toby, come ON !

375
00:23:54,814 --> 00:23:56,451
Toby, get out of there!

376
00:23:56,491 --> 00:23:59,158
Help me! Oh, my God, help me!

377
00:24:04,365 --> 00:24:06,538
It's this way!

378
00:24:18,786 --> 00:24:21,044
Hurry it up!

379
00:24:23,184 --> 00:24:25,428
Get it in. Danny, get it done.

380
00:24:25,468 --> 00:24:28,538
Transmit! I'm trying, I'm trying.
I'm getting it in. . .

381
00:24:28,578 --> 00:24:29,982
Stop them !

382
00:24:36,050 --> 00:24:38,917
Danny, get that thing transmitting!

383
00:25:00,306 --> 00:25:02,901
You did it! We did it!

384
00:25:02,941 --> 00:25:05,040
Yes! Oh, yes!

385
00:25:07,497 --> 00:25:10,814
Zack, we did it, the Ood are down!
Now we've got to get the Doctor.

386
00:25:10,854 --> 00:25:12,657
On my way!

387
00:25:13,968 --> 00:25:17,648
You get representations of the
horned beast across the universe,

388
00:25:17,688 --> 00:25:20,136
in the myths and legends
of a million worlds.

389
00:25:20,176 --> 00:25:25,079
Earth, Draconia,
Vel Consadine, Daemos,

390
00:25:25,119 --> 00:25:28,357
the Kaled God of War. . . The same
image, over and over again.

391
00:25:28,397 --> 00:25:31,791
Maybe that idea came from somewhere.

392
00:25:31,831 --> 00:25:34,267
Bleeding through.

393
00:25:34,307 --> 00:25:37,385
A thought at the back
of every sentient mind.

394
00:25:37,425 --> 00:25:39,221
Emanating from here?

395
00:25:39,261 --> 00:25:42,539
Could be. If this is the original. . .

396
00:25:42,579 --> 00:25:48,292
does that make it real, does that
make it the actual Devil, though?

397
00:25:48,332 --> 00:25:50,690
Well, if that's
what you want to believe.

398
00:25:50,730 --> 00:25:53,966
Maybe that's what the Devil is,
in the end. An idea.

399
00:25:56,816 --> 00:25:58,763
That's it.

400
00:25:58,803 --> 00:26:01,881
That's all we've got.

401
00:26:01,921 --> 00:26:04,518
You getting any sort of readout?

402
00:26:04,558 --> 00:26:06,512
Nothing.

403
00:26:06,552 --> 00:26:08,429
Could be miles to go.

404
00:26:08,469 --> 00:26:13,719
Or, could be 30 feet,
there's no way of telling.

405
00:26:15,904 --> 00:26:18,101
I could survive 30 feet.

406
00:26:18,141 --> 00:26:20,433
Oh, no, you don't,
I'm pulling you back up.

407
00:26:23,737 --> 00:26:25,664
What are you doing? !

408
00:26:25,704 --> 00:26:29,249
You bring me back, and we're just
gonna sit there and run out of air.

409
00:26:29,289 --> 00:26:31,297
I've got to go down.

410
00:26:31,337 --> 00:26:34,166
But you can't. Doctor, you can't!

411
00:26:34,206 --> 00:26:36,293
Call it an act of faith.

412
00:26:38,880 --> 00:26:41,520
I don't want to die on my own.

413
00:26:41,560 --> 00:26:44,478
I know.

414
00:26:48,788 --> 00:26:50,586
Doctor, are you there?

415
00:26:50,626 --> 00:26:52,745
Doctor? Ida? Can you hear me?

416
00:26:52,785 --> 00:26:56,180
The comms are still down. I can
patch them through the central desk

417
00:26:56,220 --> 00:26:58,808
and boost the signal. . .
Just give me a minute.

418
00:27:01,974 --> 00:27:07,170
I didn't ask. Have you got any sort
of faith, or. . . ? Not really.

419
00:27:07,210 --> 00:27:12,245
I was brought up Neo-Classic,
Congregational.

420
00:27:12,285 --> 00:27:14,577
Cos of my mum, she was. . .

421
00:27:17,881 --> 00:27:20,429
My old mum.

422
00:27:21,687 --> 00:27:23,790
But no. I never believed.

423
00:27:23,830 --> 00:27:25,839
Neo-Classics, have they got a devil?

424
00:27:25,879 --> 00:27:29,070
No.  Not as such.  Just...

425
00:27:30,184 --> 00:27:32,421
. .the things that men do.

426
00:27:32,461 --> 00:27:35,413
Same thing, in the end.
And what about you?

427
00:27:41,454 --> 00:27:45,329
I believe. . .
I believe I haven't seen everything.

428
00:27:45,369 --> 00:27:47,672
I dunno.

429
00:27:49,375 --> 00:27:51,085
Funny, isn't it?

430
00:27:51,125 --> 00:27:53,880
The things you make up. The rules.

431
00:27:53,920 --> 00:27:57,594
If that thing had said it came from
beyond the universe, I'd believe it,

432
00:27:57,634 --> 00:28:00,757
but before the universe? Impossible.

433
00:28:02,109 --> 00:28:04,816
Doesn't fit my rules.

434
00:28:07,665 --> 00:28:09,997
Still.
Maybe that's why I keep travelling.

435
00:28:12,460 --> 00:28:14,553
To be proved wrong.

436
00:28:17,737 --> 00:28:19,261
Thank you, Ida.

437
00:28:19,301 --> 00:28:22,211
Don't go!

438
00:28:22,251 --> 00:28:24,247
If they get back in touch. . .

439
00:28:24,287 --> 00:28:27,933
If you talk to Rose,
just tell her. . .

440
00:28:34,995 --> 00:28:37,088
Tell her. . .

441
00:28:40,310 --> 00:28:42,608
Oh, she knows.

442
00:28:45,664 --> 00:28:47,382
'Doctor? Are you there?

443
00:28:47,422 --> 00:28:50,269
'Doctor? Ida? Can you hear me?'

444
00:28:50,309 --> 00:28:53,045
Are you there, Doctor? He's gone.

445
00:28:54,855 --> 00:28:56,893
What d'you mean, he's gone?

446
00:28:56,933 --> 00:28:58,812
He fell.

447
00:28:58,852 --> 00:29:01,235
Into the Pit.

448
00:29:02,289 --> 00:29:05,046
I don't know how deep it is.
Miles and miles and miles.

449
00:29:05,086 --> 00:29:07,611
But. . . What d'you mean, he fell?

450
00:29:07,651 --> 00:29:10,023
I couldn't stop him.

451
00:29:13,283 --> 00:29:14,966
He said your name.

452
00:29:20,708 --> 00:29:23,541
I'm sorry.

453
00:29:25,510 --> 00:29:30,258
Ida. . .
There's no way of reaching you.

454
00:29:30,298 --> 00:29:34,895
No cable, no backup,
you're ten miles down.

455
00:29:34,935 --> 00:29:36,850
We can't get there.

456
00:29:36,890 --> 00:29:39,478
You should see this place, Zack.

457
00:29:43,772 --> 00:29:46,229
It's beautiful.

458
00:29:48,756 --> 00:29:51,748
I wanted to discover things,

459
00:29:53,951 --> 00:29:55,796
and here I am.

460
00:29:55,836 --> 00:29:57,387
We've got to abandon the base.

461
00:29:57,427 --> 00:30:00,345
I'm declaring this mission unsafe.

462
00:30:00,385 --> 00:30:04,183
All we can do is make sure
no-one ever comes here again.

463
00:30:04,223 --> 00:30:06,859
But we'll never find out what it was.

464
00:30:06,899 --> 00:30:08,576
Maybe that's best.

465
00:30:08,616 --> 00:30:10,874
Yeah.

466
00:30:14,290 --> 00:30:17,330
Officer Scott. . . It's all right.

467
00:30:17,370 --> 00:30:19,184
Just go.

468
00:30:20,733 --> 00:30:24,612
Good luck. And you.

469
00:30:29,915 --> 00:30:34,668
Danny, Toby,
close down the feed-links,
get the retrotopes online.

470
00:30:34,708 --> 00:30:37,946
Then get to the rocket and strap
yourselves in. We're leaving.

471
00:30:37,986 --> 00:30:41,541
I'm not going.
Rose, there's space for you.

472
00:30:41,581 --> 00:30:44,186
No, I'm gonna wait for the Doctor.

473
00:30:44,226 --> 00:30:45,915
Just like he'd wait for me.

474
00:30:47,575 --> 00:30:51,211
I'm sorry, but. . . he's dead.

475
00:30:51,251 --> 00:30:53,369
You don't know him.

476
00:30:53,409 --> 00:30:55,837
Cos he's not.

477
00:30:58,045 --> 00:31:00,202
I'm telling you, he's not. . .

478
00:31:00,242 --> 00:31:02,837
And even if he was,
how could I leave him?

479
00:31:02,877 --> 00:31:08,730
All on his own, all the way
down there? No, I'm gonna stay.

480
00:31:10,311 --> 00:31:12,748
Then. . . I apologise for this.

481
00:31:12,788 --> 00:31:14,825
Danny, Toby, make her secure.

482
00:31:14,865 --> 00:31:17,584
No! No! No! Stop! STOP!

483
00:31:17,624 --> 00:31:20,667
Let me go! GET OFF ME!
I'm not leaving!

484
00:31:23,821 --> 00:31:25,901
I've lost too many people.

485
00:31:25,941 --> 00:31:28,643
I'm not leaving you behind.

486
00:31:29,893 --> 00:31:32,566
Let's get her on board.

487
00:31:35,888 --> 00:31:37,650
Did that one just move?

488
00:31:37,690 --> 00:31:40,719
It's the telepathic field,
it's reasserting itself!

489
00:31:40,759 --> 00:31:42,641
Move it, get to the rocket, move!

490
00:31:50,555 --> 00:31:52,762
Ughhh. . .

491
00:32:02,023 --> 00:32:04,560
I'm breathing!

492
00:32:10,889 --> 00:32:13,187
Air cushion to support the fall.

493
00:32:14,206 --> 00:32:17,120
You can breathe down here, Ida!

494
00:32:17,160 --> 00:32:18,880
Can you hear me, Ida?

495
00:32:18,920 --> 00:32:23,555
Dislocating B clamp, C clamp.
raising blu-nitro to maximum.
How's the negapact feed line?

496
00:32:23,595 --> 00:32:27,148
Clear, ready to go, sir. Oh, for
God's sake, get us out of here!

497
00:32:27,188 --> 00:32:30,505
Captain. Think we're gonna have
a problem. Keep an eye on her.

498
00:32:30,545 --> 00:32:33,982
What did you. . . ?
It's all right, Rose, we're safe.

499
00:32:34,022 --> 00:32:39,511
I'm not going anywhere! Get me
out of this thing. . . Get me OUT!
Aaaaand, lift off!

500
00:32:53,719 --> 00:32:55,812
The rocket!

501
00:33:02,033 --> 00:33:04,750
Take me back to the planet.

502
00:33:04,790 --> 00:33:07,187
Take me back! Or what?

503
00:33:07,227 --> 00:33:09,280
Or I'll shoot.

504
00:33:11,741 --> 00:33:13,824
Would you, though?

505
00:33:13,864 --> 00:33:17,840
Would you really?
Is that what your Doctor would want?

506
00:33:24,249 --> 00:33:27,207
I'm sorry. But it's too late,
anyway. Take a look outside.

507
00:33:27,247 --> 00:33:29,844
We can't turn back.

508
00:33:29,884 --> 00:33:33,735
And this is what the Doctor
would have wanted, isn't that right?

509
00:33:38,837 --> 00:33:42,268
History of some big battle. . .
Man against Beast.

510
00:33:42,308 --> 00:33:44,666
Dunno if you're getting this, Ida.
Hope so.

511
00:33:44,706 --> 00:33:48,636
Anyway, they defeated the Beast,
and imprisoned it.

512
00:33:56,781 --> 00:33:58,988
And maybe that's the key.

513
00:34:06,486 --> 00:34:09,239
Or the gate, or the bars, or. . .

514
00:34:32,338 --> 00:34:35,976
What's the joke? Just. . . We made it!

515
00:34:36,016 --> 00:34:38,295
We escaped! We actually did it!

516
00:34:38,335 --> 00:34:40,650
Not all of us.
We're not out of it yet.

517
00:34:40,690 --> 00:34:44,760
we're still the first people
in history to fly away
from a black hole.

518
00:34:44,800 --> 00:34:46,560
Toby, read me the stats.

519
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:48,718
Gravity funnel holding, sir.

520
00:34:48,758 --> 00:34:50,395
Ohh, it's holding!

521
00:34:50,435 --> 00:34:52,595
I accept that you exist.

522
00:34:52,635 --> 00:34:57,869
I don't have to accept what you are,
but your physical existence,
I give you that.

523
00:35:00,346 --> 00:35:04,184
I don't understand.
I was expected down here.

524
00:35:04,224 --> 00:35:08,217
I was given a safe landing, and air.

525
00:35:08,257 --> 00:35:10,674
You need me for something -
what for?

526
00:35:15,732 --> 00:35:18,049
Have I got to. . . ?

527
00:35:18,089 --> 00:35:20,009
I don't know, beg an audience,
or. . . ?

528
00:35:20,049 --> 00:35:22,005
Is there a ritual?

529
00:35:22,045 --> 00:35:25,240
Some sort of incantation
or summons or spell?

530
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:28,073
All those things I don't believe in,
are they real?

531
00:35:29,394 --> 00:35:32,227
Speak to me! Tell me!

532
00:35:35,431 --> 00:35:37,748
You won't talk.

533
00:35:37,788 --> 00:35:40,584
Or. . .you can't talk.

534
00:35:43,301 --> 00:35:47,256
Hold on, hold on, wait a minute,
just let me. . .

535
00:35:47,296 --> 00:35:48,856
Oh! No.

536
00:35:48,896 --> 00:35:50,773
Yes! No.

537
00:35:50,813 --> 00:35:54,570
Think it through! You spoke
before, I heard your voice.

538
00:35:54,610 --> 00:35:58,131
An intelligent voice.
No, more than that, brilliant.

539
00:35:59,921 --> 00:36:04,558
But looking at you now,
all I can see. . .

540
00:36:07,195 --> 00:36:10,992
. . is the Beast.

541
00:36:11,032 --> 00:36:12,949
The animal.

542
00:36:12,989 --> 00:36:15,107
Just. . .the body.

543
00:36:15,147 --> 00:36:19,145
You're just the body, the physical
form. What happened to your mind?

544
00:36:19,185 --> 00:36:21,540
Hmm?

545
00:36:21,580 --> 00:36:24,862
Were's it gone?
Where's that intelligence?

546
00:36:28,335 --> 00:36:30,462
Oh no. . .

547
00:36:32,093 --> 00:36:37,002
Stats at 53, funnel stable at 66.5,
hull pressure constant.

548
00:36:37,042 --> 00:36:40,360
Smooth as we can, sir,
all the way back home.

549
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:42,487
Co-ordinates set for Planet Earth.

550
00:36:44,074 --> 00:36:46,907
You're imprisoned, long time ago.

551
00:36:47,954 --> 00:36:51,627
Before the universe, after,
sideways, in between,
doesn't matter.

552
00:36:51,667 --> 00:36:54,225
And the prison is perfect.

553
00:36:54,265 --> 00:36:56,862
It's absolute, it's eternal. . .

554
00:36:56,902 --> 00:36:58,582
Oh, yes.

555
00:36:58,622 --> 00:37:02,496
Open the prison,
and the gravity field collapses,

556
00:37:02,536 --> 00:37:05,988
this planet
falls into the black hole.

557
00:37:07,016 --> 00:37:09,331
You escape, you die. Brilliant!

558
00:37:09,371 --> 00:37:11,448
But that's just the body.

559
00:37:11,488 --> 00:37:14,155
The body's trapped, that's all.

560
00:37:15,681 --> 00:37:20,152
The Devil is an idea, in all
those civilisations, just an idea.

561
00:37:21,315 --> 00:37:24,033
But an idea is hard to kill.

562
00:37:24,073 --> 00:37:26,661
An idea can escape!

563
00:37:28,111 --> 00:37:33,704
The mind, the mind of the great
Beast, the mind can escape.

564
00:37:33,744 --> 00:37:36,381
Oh, but that's it!

565
00:37:36,421 --> 00:37:38,538
You didn't give me air.
Your jailers did!

566
00:37:38,578 --> 00:37:41,858
They set this up,
all those years ago.

567
00:37:41,898 --> 00:37:44,536
They need me alive!

568
00:37:44,576 --> 00:37:47,853
Because if you're escaping
then I've got to stop you.

569
00:37:53,164 --> 00:37:56,160
If I destroy your prison,
your body is destroyed.

570
00:37:56,200 --> 00:37:58,492
Your mind with it?

571
00:38:06,189 --> 00:38:10,026
But then you're clever enough to
use this whole system against me.

572
00:38:10,066 --> 00:38:14,781
If I destroy this planet,
then I destroy the gravity field.

573
00:38:15,700 --> 00:38:19,578
The rocket.
The rocket loses protection.

574
00:38:19,618 --> 00:38:21,421
Falls into the Black Hole.

575
00:38:23,971 --> 00:38:26,519
I have to sacrifice Rose.

576
00:38:33,199 --> 00:38:35,596
It doesn't make sense.

577
00:38:35,636 --> 00:38:38,916
We escaped, but there's a thousand
ways it could've killed us.

578
00:38:38,956 --> 00:38:44,547
It could've ripped out the air,
or burnt us, or anything,

579
00:38:44,587 --> 00:38:46,799
But it let us go - why?

580
00:38:48,304 --> 00:38:50,341
Unless it wanted us to escape.

581
00:38:50,381 --> 00:38:52,741
Hey, Rose, do us a favour.

582
00:38:52,781 --> 00:38:54,584
Shut up.

583
00:38:55,578 --> 00:39:00,332
Almost there. We're beyond the
reach of the Black Hole in 40, 39. . .

584
00:39:00,372 --> 00:39:02,290
So that's the trap.

585
00:39:02,330 --> 00:39:05,362
Or the test or the final judgement,
I don't know.

586
00:39:07,124 --> 00:39:09,627
But if I kill you, I kill her.

587
00:39:14,198 --> 00:39:16,955
Except that implies,

588
00:39:16,995 --> 00:39:20,509
in this big, grand scheme
of gods and devils,

589
00:39:20,549 --> 00:39:22,948
she's just a victim.

590
00:39:22,988 --> 00:39:25,706
But I've seen a lot of the universe.

591
00:39:25,746 --> 00:39:28,742
I've seen fake gods, and bad gods,

592
00:39:28,782 --> 00:39:30,780
and demi-gods and would-be gods,

593
00:39:30,820 --> 00:39:34,857
and out of all that,
out of that whole pantheon,

594
00:39:34,897 --> 00:39:36,973
if I believe in one thing,

595
00:39:37,013 --> 00:39:39,350
just one thing. . .

596
00:39:40,371 --> 00:39:42,783
I believe in her.

597
00:39:47,242 --> 00:39:49,920
What was that?
What's he doing? What is he doing? !

598
00:39:49,960 --> 00:39:52,476
We've lost the funnel!
Gravity collapse!

599
00:39:52,516 --> 00:39:54,593
What does that mean?
We can't escape!

600
00:39:54,633 --> 00:39:57,710
We're heading straight
for the black hole!

601
00:40:06,221 --> 00:40:08,060
This is your freedom !

602
00:40:08,100 --> 00:40:10,779
Free to die!

603
00:40:10,819 --> 00:40:14,055
You're going into the black hole,
and I'm riding with you!

604
00:40:19,210 --> 00:40:22,924
It's the planet,
the planet's moving!

605
00:40:22,964 --> 00:40:25,097
It's falling.

606
00:40:26,678 --> 00:40:30,394
I am the rage and the bile
and the ferocity!

607
00:40:30,434 --> 00:40:33,712
I am the prince and the fool
and the agony! It's him, it's Toby!

608
00:40:33,752 --> 00:40:37,670
I am the sin and the fear and the
darkness! The ship's not stable!

609
00:40:37,710 --> 00:40:40,093
What is he? What the hell is he? !

610
00:40:43,344 --> 00:40:45,060
I shall never die!

611
00:40:45,100 --> 00:40:46,820
The thought of me is for ever!

612
00:40:46,860 --> 00:40:51,255
In the bleeding hearts of men, in
their vanity and obsession and lust!

613
00:40:51,295 --> 00:40:54,492
Nothing shall ever destroy me!
Nothing!

614
00:40:54,532 --> 00:40:56,790
Go to hell.

615
00:41:07,317 --> 00:41:09,979
Emergency shield!

616
00:41:18,625 --> 00:41:20,582
We've still lost the gravity funnel.

617
00:41:20,622 --> 00:41:22,303
We can't escape the black hole.

618
00:41:22,343 --> 00:41:25,419
But we stopped him. That's
what the Doctor would have done.

619
00:41:25,459 --> 00:41:29,150
Some victory. We're going in. . .

620
00:41:44,958 --> 00:41:48,155
The planet's lost orbit.
It's falling!

621
00:42:14,723 --> 00:42:17,443
The planet's gone.

622
00:42:17,483 --> 00:42:20,150
I'm sorry. Accelerating.

623
00:42:20,640 --> 00:42:23,277
I did my best.

624
00:42:23,317 --> 00:42:28,110
But hey, first human beings
to fall inside a black hole,

625
00:42:28,150 --> 00:42:30,548
how about that?

626
00:42:30,588 --> 00:42:33,130
History.

627
00:42:44,258 --> 00:42:47,204
What happened?

628
00:42:51,284 --> 00:42:54,122
We're turning.

629
00:42:54,162 --> 00:42:55,882
We're turning around.

630
00:42:55,922 --> 00:42:57,998
We're turning away!

631
00:42:59,836 --> 00:43:03,952
'Sorry about the hijack, Captain.
This is the good ship Tardis. '

632
00:43:03,992 --> 00:43:07,030
Now, first things first,
have you got a Rose Tyler on board?

633
00:43:07,070 --> 00:43:08,907
I'm here! It's me!

634
00:43:08,947 --> 00:43:11,108
Oh, my God! Where are you?

635
00:43:11,148 --> 00:43:13,025
I'm just towing you home.

636
00:43:13,065 --> 00:43:16,581
Gravity, shmavity - my people
practically invented black holes.

637
00:43:16,621 --> 00:43:19,698
In fact, they did. Couple of
minutes, we'll be nice and safe.

638
00:43:19,738 --> 00:43:22,135
Oh, and Captain? Can we do a swap?

639
00:43:22,175 --> 00:43:27,207
Say, if you give me Rose Tyler, I'll
give you Ida Scott, how about that?

640
00:43:27,247 --> 00:43:30,444
She's alive? ! Thank God.

641
00:43:30,484 --> 00:43:33,680
Yeah, bit of oxygen starvation,
but she should be all right.

642
00:43:33,720 --> 00:43:35,717
I couldn't save the Ood.

643
00:43:35,757 --> 00:43:38,358
I only had time for one trip.

644
00:43:38,398 --> 00:43:40,755
They went down with the planet.

645
00:43:43,111 --> 00:43:44,911
Entering clear space.

646
00:43:44,951 --> 00:43:47,368
End of the line. Mission closed.

647
00:44:06,284 --> 00:44:10,322
'I don't know, I can't remember. '

648
00:44:10,362 --> 00:44:12,479
Well, it looked like a box!

649
00:44:12,519 --> 00:44:14,277
What d'you mean, a box?

650
00:44:14,317 --> 00:44:18,113
Down in the hold. A big blue box.

651
00:44:18,153 --> 00:44:21,111
It just appeared - I don't know!

652
00:44:21,151 --> 00:44:25,428
'Zack, we'll be off now.
Have a good trip home. '

653
00:44:25,468 --> 00:44:28,784
And the next time
you get curious about something. . .

654
00:44:28,824 --> 00:44:32,779
Oh, what's the point?
You'll just go blundering in.

655
00:44:32,819 --> 00:44:36,935
The human race! But Doctor. . .
what did you find down there?

656
00:44:36,975 --> 00:44:39,170
That creature, what was it?

657
00:44:39,210 --> 00:44:42,487
I don't know.
Never did decipher that writing.

658
00:44:42,527 --> 00:44:46,644
But that's good! Day I know
everything, I might as well stop.

659
00:44:46,684 --> 00:44:48,960
What do you think it was? Really?

660
00:44:49,000 --> 00:44:52,078
I think. . .we beat it.

661
00:44:52,118 --> 00:44:55,559
That's good enough for me. It said
I was going to die in battle.

662
00:44:57,872 --> 00:44:59,555
Then it lied.

663
00:45:01,030 --> 00:45:03,746
Right! Onwards! Upwards! Ida. . .

664
00:45:03,786 --> 00:45:06,104
see you again, maybe. I ope so.

665
00:45:06,144 --> 00:45:07,904
And thanks, boys!

666
00:45:07,944 --> 00:45:11,738
Hang on though, Doctor.
You never really said. . .

667
00:45:11,778 --> 00:45:14,737
You two. . .who are you?

668
00:45:14,777 --> 00:45:18,662
Oh. . .the stuff of legend.

669
00:45:21,565 --> 00:45:25,802
This is the final report
of Sanctuary Base Six.

670
00:45:25,842 --> 00:45:28,959
Officer Tobias Zed.

671
00:45:28,999 --> 00:45:34,314
Deceased, with honours, 43K 2.1.

672
00:45:34,354 --> 00:45:40,948
Also. . . Ood 1 alpha 1, deceased,
with honours.

673
00:45:40,988 --> 00:45:46,523
Ood 1 alpha 2, deceased,
with honours. . .

674
00:45:50,976 --> 00:45:52,813
deceased, with honours,

675
00:45:52,853 --> 00:45:53,393
43K 2.1.

676
00:45:55,053 --> 00:45:56,327
43K 2.1.

677
00:45:56,527 --> 00:45:59,007
I am your salvation.

678
00:45:59,047 --> 00:46:03,103
The sound of the universe.
What does it mean?

679
00:46:03,961 --> 00:46:05,999
His name is The Doctor. Doctor what?

680
00:46:06,039 --> 00:46:07,523
Find me that girl!

681
00:46:09,675 --> 00:46:12,832
Here we are, strangers,
and I'm flashing you me knickers!

682
00:46:12,872 --> 00:46:15,149
One step closer
to catching the Doctor.

683
00:46:15,189 --> 00:46:17,367
Don't I know you?

684
00:46:34,809 --> 00:46:40,917
